                <tr>
                    <td><span class="keyword-term">Encapsulation</span></td>
                    <td>Level C: Inventory uses a protected list; access through methods</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td><span class="keyword-term">Inheritance</span></td>
                    <td>Level B: Brute and Scout inherit from Player</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td><span class="keyword-term">Overriding</span></td>
                    <td>Level B: Brute and Scout override a method to describe their specialty</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td><span class="keyword-term">Polymorphism</span></td>
                    <td>Level B: Same method name, different class behavior</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td><span class="keyword-term">Composition</span></td>
                    <td>Level C: Player has an Inventory</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td><span class="keyword-term">Aggregation</span></td>
                    <td>Concept only: one object uses another without owning it</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td><span class="keyword-term">Abstraction</span></td>
                    <td>Concept only: the engine expects methods to exist, not how they are made</td>
                </tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>
    </div>
</section>

